//
// Both paths are lazy and reduce once per coefficient, so the comparison comes
// down to product count and Karatsuba wins. This depends on the relaxed
// [fr.LazyMul] contract: Karatsuba's cross terms multiply non-canonical sums,
// and having to reduce those first is what made it lose to schoolbook before.
